<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine 8-mth BOP surplus rises to $3.995 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippine 8-mth BOP surplus rises to $3.995 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines posted a balance of payments surplus of $3.995 billion in the first eight months of 1996 against a $1.02 billion surplus in the same period last year, the Central Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Central Bank director for research Diwa Gunigundo said the increased surplus was primarily due to higher inflows of foreign investments and strong foreign exchange remittances.</p>
</text>
